>> title: Whitefish Salad
>> category: Salads
>> tags: smoked fish, mayonnaise, no-cook, appetizing, deli
>> counters: Deli
>> aka: smoked whitefish salad, chub salad, whitefish, whitefish spread, smoked fish salad
>> pairs-with: bagels, cream-cheese, scallion-schmear
>> servings: 6
>> time: 2 hr 20 min
>> slack: narrow — smoked fish and mayonnaise is a three-day item in the fridge and it is not a counter one; the two-hour chill is what firms it, and the flakes are folded rather than stirred because once they break down it is a paste and there is no unbreaking them
>> step.1: debone the whitefish, keep the flakes big
>> step.2: whisk the dressing
>> step.3: fold in the celery and dill
>> step.4: chill 2 hr

Skin @whole smoked whitefish{1 1/2%lb}(680 g; a golden chub from the fish case, bought smoked) and lift the meat off the frame in the largest pieces it will give you, going over every piece twice for pin bones. A pound and a half on the bone is about half a pound of meat, which is why the tub costs what it costs. The fish is bought smoked: hot-smoking a whitefish at home is a smokehouse job, not a kitchen one.

Whisk @mayonnaise{1/3%cup}(80 mL), @sour cream{2%Tbs}, @lemon juice{2%tsp}, @black pepper{1/4%tsp} and @cayenne{1%pinch} together. Smoked fish is already salted, so nothing here carries salt — taste at the end and you will usually find it does not want any.

Fold @&(~1)dressing{} into @&(~2)picked whitefish{} with @celery{1%rib}(diced fine), @red onion{2%Tbs}(diced fine) and @fresh dill{2%Tbs}(chopped), turning it over just enough to coat. Half of what people like about this is the size of the flakes, and it takes about four extra turns of the spoon to lose them.

Chill @&(~1)whitefish salad{} ~chill{2%hr}. On a bagel with tomato and onion, or in a scoop on the appetizing platter beside the lox and the schmear. Three days, and it is best on the second.
